// ⚠️ DEVELOPER DOCUMENTATION - MUST READ BEFORE MODIFYING ⚠️
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// Comprehensive developer documentation is available in:
// ./DTT_SESSION_DEVELOPER_DOCS.md
//
// READ THIS DOCUMENTATION BEFORE MAKING ANY CHANGES TO THIS FILE!
//
// The documentation covers:
// - Business requirements & expectations (session accuracy across timeframes)
// - Critical implementation details (ROOT CAUSE fixes for midnight-wrapping)
// - Common pitfalls & how to avoid them
// - Architecture decisions & rationale
// - Mandatory testing requirements
// - Modification checklist (22-point verification before commits)
//
// Key reminders:
// ✓ Session highs/lows MUST match exactly across all timeframes (1m-5m)
// ✓ Test Nagasaki & Turncoat sessions on 3-minute charts (midnight wrapping)
// ✓ Do NOT change initialization values (-1e10, 1e10)
// ✓ Do NOT modify time_in_bar_range() without understanding ROOT CAUSE fix
// ✓ Do NOT remove 1-minute bar filtering (lines 620-659)
// ✓ Always use local variable copies in session loops
// ✓ Visual elements (boundaries/lines) must draw at SESSION START, not root time
// ✓ Check `not na(session_start_timestamp)` before drawing visual elements
//
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// CHANGELOG - Record of all changes and WHY they were made
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// [2025-10-13] - Fixed label and boundary timing for pre-created sessions
// PROBLEM: Model 111 label appeared at 13:30 (root time) instead of 14:09 (start time)
//          Model 1001 end boundary disappeared at 13:30 when Model 111 was pre-created
// ROOT CAUSE: Visual elements were drawing during pre-creation instead of session start
// FIX: Added `not na(session_start_timestamp)` checks before drawing visual elements
//      Only delete previous boundary when session officially starts, not during pre-creation
// LOCATIONS: Lines 608, 515-526, 564-584, 641
// TEST: Model 111 label must appear at 14:09, Model 1001 boundary must stay until 14:09
//
// [2025-10-13] - Fixed end_timestamp calculation bug
// PROBLEM: Lines extending 24 hours into future when changing "Show Last N Days"
// ROOT CAUSE: `if end_timestamp <= time` incorrectly added a day for historical sessions
// FIX: Only add day if session wraps midnight, not if end_timestamp is in the past
// LOCATIONS: Lines 549, 574, 661
// TEST: Change "Show Last N Days" to 2, verify lines don't extend into tomorrow
//
// [2025-10-13] - Added fallback for empty intrabar data
// PROBLEM: request.security_lower_tf() returns empty arrays on real-time bars/chart load
// ROOT CAUSE: TradingView data availability issues
// FIX: If array empty, push current bar's high/low/time as fallback
// LOCATION: Lines 724-728
// TEST: Big Ben and NY Open high/low lines must appear on fresh chart load
//
// [2025-10-13] - Reverted session initialization to extreme values
// PROBLEM: Using `high, low` could capture wrong values if session starts mid-bar
// ROOT CAUSE: Session might start at 9:30 but bar covers 9:28-9:33, so high/low includes pre-session data
// FIX: Keep -1e10, 1e10 initialization so first 1-minute data always overwrites
// LOCATION: Line 613
// TEST: Session highs/lows must match across all timeframes (1m-5m)
//
// [2025-10-13] - CRITICAL BUG FIX: Separated root capture from root display
// PROBLEM: Root data wouldn't be captured when "Show Root Prices" toggle was OFF
// ROOT CAUSE: Root CAPTURE was gated by `if show_roots` at line 832
// FIX: Changed to `if true` - root capture now ALWAYS happens, display toggle only affects visualization
// LOCATION: Line 834 (changed from `if show_roots` to `if true`)
// TEST: Turn OFF "Show Root Prices", root data should still be captured (future AMRP will need this)
// WHY CRITICAL: Separation of concerns - data capture MUST be independent of display preferences
//
// [2025-10-13] - CRITICAL BUG FIX: Validate session high/low before drawing lines
// PROBLEM: Judas and NY Open missing high/low lines on 1-minute chart ONLY
// ROOT CAUSE: Previous sessions (Big Ben, NY Open) had high/low still at initialization values (-1e10, 1e10)
//             These pass `not na()` check but are invalid data that draw lines off-screen
// FIX: Added validation: high < 1e9 AND low > -1e9 (realistic price ranges)
// LOCATIONS: Lines 560-562 (phase 2), Lines 693-695 (session creation)
// TEST: Load 1-minute chart, Judas and NY Open should show high/low lines
// WHY 1-MIN ONLY: On higher timeframes (2m+), request.security_lower_tf() returns data properly
//                 On 1-minute, it may return empty arrays, leaving sessions at initialization values
//
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
